From a3abbf7f7c37fa97dcf3c25cba781680cf0b8ca7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:51:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix audit 447bb70d: repurchase, 409/422, grant form, backup
 wording

- vault.prepare: a request id that finds a failed run renames that row's
  request id, as retire_lapsed does, so a page restored from history
  can buy the refunded reading again. The failed row keeps its id and
  order for late delivery and refunds.
- paid.py: IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT answers 409 and request refusals 422
  instead of 503 STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE; the page drops its kept id on 409.
- Grant form: no signature for an amount above grantLeft or with no
  grant left; GRANT_DAILY_LIMIT no longer says the limit is reached.
- Privacy text: backups are deleted by the operator by hand.

Touches the wallet lock (paid.py, WorldGoldPanel.tsx); hashes not
refreshed, so a new Swarm audit is required before release.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
